# find: library calls (sinh, cosh, tanh and their inverses) as exp, log
# and sqrt, the special-function unit's instructions: the formula Vulkan
# inherits each one's precision from, and a form with one exp; each
# priced under gt1030 and measured against the call
use gt1030
f(x: f32 in -4..4) = tanh(x)
find f 1
s(x: f32 in 0.5..4) = sinh(x)
find s 1
c(x: f32 in -4..4) = cosh(x)
find c 1
as(x: f32 in -4..4) = asinh(x)
find as 1
ac(x: f32 in 1..8) = acosh(x)
find ac 1
at(x: f32 in -0.9..0.9) = atanh(x)
find at 1
# a tone curve of two inputs: the calls inside an expression
tm(x: f32 in 0..20, w: f32 in 1..2) = tanh(x * w) * 0.5 + 0.5
find tm
# where exp overflows the inherited formula is NaN, the one-exp form is not
big(x: f32 in -100..100) = tanh(x)
find big 1
